{
  "title": "把太陽請出來",
  "title_en": "Inviting the Sun",
  "series": "神話未完成",
  "series_en": "Myths in the Making",
  "volume": 4,
  "model": "史旺姬",
  "creator": "史旺基 Swanky",
  "slug": "swanky-ji-inviting-the-sun",
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "count": 36,
  "cover_photo": 28,
  "setting": "沒有封上的洞口",
  "lead": "當一個人不願意走出來，我們能給她什麼？",
  "lead_en": "What can we offer someone who does not want to come out?",
  "statement": "當一個人不願意走出來，我們能給她什麼？\n\n《古事記》記載，天照隱入岩戶，天地陷入黑暗；天宇受賣在門外表演，眾神大笑。天照探身看鏡時，天手力男將她牽出；布刀玉在她身後拉起繩，告訴她不可再退回去。\n\n這裡的重心在門外那群不太會表演的人：敲木箱的拍子會錯，舉起的枝葉被火光投成一隻巨大的鳥。笑聲抵達石壁，卻沒有替她決定下一步。後來，他們學會放輕聲音、讓出位置。\n\n鏡子不是命令，只是一面被搬到空地上的鏡架。她伸手改變它的角度，那是她自己的決定。\n\n從岩室的冷，到門外的火光、草坡上的日光，最後停在溪邊的休息。走向光，不表示從此必須快樂。\n\n洞口一直開著。她仍選擇追上同伴；因為還能回去，走出來才是選擇。",
  "statement_en": "What can we offer someone who does not want to come out?\n\nIn the Kojiki, Amaterasu hides in the rock cave and the world goes dark. Amenouzume performs outside and the gods laugh. As Amaterasu leans out to look at the mirror, Amenotajikarao draws her out; Futodama stretches a rope behind her and tells her not to retreat again.\n\nHere the weight shifts to the people outside, who are not very good at performing: their beat on a wooden crate goes wrong, and the branches they raise are thrown by firelight into the shadow of an enormous bird. Their laughter reaches the rock wall but does not decide her next step. Slowly they learn to lower their voices and make room.\n\nThe mirror is not a command, only a mirror on a stand, carried out into a clearing. She reaches out and changes its angle; the decision is hers.\n\nFrom the cold of the cave to the firelight at its mouth, the daylight on the grassy slope and, at last, a rest by the stream: walking toward the light does not oblige her to be happy.\n\nThe cave stays open. She still chooses to catch up with her companions; only because she can go back is walking out a choice.",
  "series_statement": "《神話未完成》\n史旺姬走進流傳至今的神話，留下它最核心的問題，讓它面對今天的生活。神話一直被講述、被使用，所以還沒有完成。",
  "series_statement_en": "Myths in the Making\nSwanky Ji steps into myths that are still being told, keeps the question at their heart, and lets it meet the life we live now. A myth that is still told and still used is not yet finished.",
  "story_zh": "故事從天照隱入岩戶的神話出發。光的退隱、門外的表演與鏡子的出現，讓我們思考人如何重新與世界相遇。\n在這次改寫中，史旺姬不是等待被帶走的人；她聽見、觀看，最後自己決定靠近。枝影喜劇、溪邊休息與不封閉洞口的結尾，是本作為這份選擇留下的想像。",
  "story_en": "The story begins with the myth of Amaterasu withdrawing into the rock cave. The retreat of light, the performance outside and the appearance of a mirror offer ways to think about meeting the world again.\nIn this adaptation, Swanky Ji listens and watches before choosing to approach. The shadow comedy, the streamside rest and the entrance left unsealed are inventions that make space for her choice.",
  "sources_zh": "故事參考：《古事記》上卷岩戶段，Basil Hall Chamberlain 1882年英譯第XVI節；國學院大學《神道事典》天照、天宇受賣與石凝姥條目。",
  "sources_en": "Story references: Kojiki, the rock-cave episode, section XVI of Basil Hall Chamberlain's 1882 English translation; Kokugakuin University's Encyclopedia of Shinto entries on Amaterasu, Amenouzume and Ishikoridome.",
  "chapters": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "title": "留一點暗",
      "title_en": "Room for Darkness",
      "text": "她把椅子挪開。外面有人把拍子敲錯了。",
      "text_en": "She moves the chair away. Outside, someone misses a beat."
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "title": "笑聲不是命令",
      "title_en": "Laughter Is Not a Command",
      "text": "笑聲抵達石壁，沒有替她決定下一步。",
      "text_en": "Laughter reaches the stone. It does not decide her next step."
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "title": "把聲音放輕",
      "title_en": "A Quieter Invitation",
      "text": "邀請停在洞外。她向光走近一步。",
      "text_en": "The invitation waits outside. She takes a step toward the light."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "看見與被看見",
      "title_en": "Seeing and Being Seen",
      "text": "鏡子被搬到空地。她開始伸手，改變它的位置。",
      "text_en": "The mirror is carried into the clearing. She reaches out to adjust its position."
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "同行與停歇",
      "title_en": "Walking and Resting",
      "text": "她與同伴走上草坡，再一起停在溪邊。",
      "text_en": "She walks uphill with her companions. Together, they pause beside the stream."
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "留著回身的地方",
      "title_en": "Leaving Room to Turn Back",
      "text": "洞口沒有封住。她仍選擇追上他們。",
      "text_en": "The entrance remains open. She still chooses to catch up."
    }
  ],
